Requirements:
- Name: `clampLonLat`
- Input: `{ lon: number; lat: number }`
- Output: `{ lon: number; lat: number }`
- Clamp longitude to [-180, 180]
- Clamp latitude to [-90, 90]
- If input is not finite numbers, throw `TypeError('invalid lon/lat')`
- Pure function, no side effects
- No dependencies
```typescript
function clampLonLat({ lon, lat }: { lon: number; lat: number }): { lon: number; lat: number } {
  if (!Number.isFinite(lon) || !Number.isFinite(lat)) {
    throw new TypeError('invalid lon/lat');
  }
  return {
    lon: Math.max(-180, Math.min(180, lon)),
    lat: Math.max(-90, Math.min(90, lat))
  };
}
```

Klammert Koordinaten in gültige Geo-Bereiche und validiert Eingabewerte.
